WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Team energy is a shared operating constraint.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.680
A group can have enough people and still lack the collective capacity for good execution

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.380
if communication load is too high,

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:12.845
ownership is unclear, meetings are excessive, or interruption culture prevents focus.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:15.510
Team performance is not only a sum of individual motivation.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:19.845
It is shaped by the system that distributes attention, decisions, and recovery.

00:00:19.845 --> 00:00:21.195
Communication load deserves careful design.

00:00:21.195 --> 00:00:23.915
Too little communication creates confusion and rework.

00:00:23.915 --> 00:00:26.599
Too much communication creates noise and constant checking.

00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:30.800
Clear ownership reduces energy drain because people know who decides, who contributes,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.950
who needs to be informed, and where escalation should go.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.790
Escalation paths matter because unresolved uncertainty can consume attention across an

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:38.835
entire team.

00:00:38.835 --> 00:00:43.120
Psychological safety at a practical level means people can raise risks, ask questions,

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.140
admit uncertainty,

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:47.840
and challenge assumptions without unnecessary punishment or humiliation.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:48.980
This is not softness.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.755
It is a reliability mechanism.

00:00:50.755 --> 00:00:53.870
Teams waste less energy hiding problems when they can discuss them early.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.960
They also make better decisions when people can surface constraints before those

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.755
constraints become failures.

00:00:58.755 --> 00:01:02.080
Sustainable pace reduces reliance on heroic individual effort.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.880
Heroics may be necessary during a real incident,

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.755
but they should not become the standard operating model.

00:01:06.755 --> 00:01:09.705
Protecting focus time, respecting recovery and non-work commitments,

00:01:09.705 --> 00:01:11.180
reducing unnecessary meetings,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.426
and clarifying priorities all help teams use energy more wisely.

00:01:14.426 --> 00:01:18.640
A team that treats energy as shared capacity can execute more reliably without burning

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.320
people down.
